    "explanation": "To both parties: this dispute over the SGD 4.50 no-show fee goes to a human reviewer, because the one fact the fee turns on cannot be decided on this record. Escalation (POL-NS-09) is terminal: I issue no refund and no compensation, and the disputed SGD 4.50 is held - neither collected from the rider nor refunded to him - while the review is pending.\n\nWhat is settled. The driver accepted the trip at 11:28:17, tapped 'arrived' at 11:32:47 and cancelled at 11:39:28 under the code RIDER_NO_SHOW, a limb (d) code of POL-NS-01. The rider never boarded and the chat log holds 0 messages, so POL-NS-04 cannot run (its limb (a) needs a rider message and there is none); POL-NS-11 says the absent rider track is neutral and decides nothing, and I did not treat it as fault. The fare line of SGD 4.50 equals the SGD 4.50 in force, so there is no fare-integrity defect (POL-NS-08(d)). POL-NS-05 is not engaged: the arrival tap fired at the very first in-geofence fix, 11:32:47 (dwell_start_offset_sec 0.0), so no false-arrival referral is issued. The anti-farming check does not trip (0 no-show terminations against 85 completed trips in 30 days), and nothing in either party's history escalates this (0 and 0 repeat pairings; 0 rider no-show disputes in 30 days).\n\nThe undecided fact. Whether the driver held position inside the 50 m pickup radius for a continuous 180 seconds (POL-NS-01(c)). That rests on EV-GPS-02756, and I say both things about it, as POL-GEN-02 requires: at the pre-pass level it is impaired at weight_multiplier 0.39 for issue codes GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW and LOW_COVERAGE, and at policy level it is impaired under POL-NS-08(b), because it contains a 197-second sampling gap (11:33:47 to 11:37:04) inside the waiting window, longer than the 120-second threshold.\n\nThe impaired stretch is the pivot. On the recorded fixes the driver's longest uninterrupted in-geofence run is 143 seconds - 37 seconds short of the 180-second minimum - and the 60-second and 143-second intervals cannot be added together, because POL-NS-06(i) permits summation only with a present and populated traffic advisory and EV-ADVIS-02756-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, carrying no fact for anyone). But the 197-second hole is exactly the stretch that could contain the missing 37 seconds, and the trace shows nothing there. The 0.0 km straight-line separation across the gap is a lower bound, not proof the driver stayed inside the radius, and the derived block's own 400-second 'longest qualifying run' is a span across that hole, not a measured continuous dwell. So the driver's account ('I waited the full time') and the trip record's 6.7-minute wait timer do not fill the hole: the wait timer runs from the driver's own arrival tap, whereas POL-NS-01(c) measures the dwell from the first qualifying in-geofence fix and not from the tap, and POL-NS-12 makes the platform's own events an independent carrier only where the arrival marker is GPS_AUTO - this trip's marker is BUTTON. The trip record therefore neither lifts the confidence cap nor stops the impaired trace from being the only evidence of the dwell. The rider's 143-second shortfall finding fails for the same reason: it rests solely on the same impaired artifact and cannot be affirmed while the gap is unobserved. Neither side's reading therefore supports a money ruling.\n\nTriggers. POL-NS-09(e): the sole evidence for the deciding fact is impaired under POL-NS-08(b). POL-NS-09(a): my confidence is capped at 0.39 by the only artifact carrying the deciding fact, below the 0.70 floor.\n\nOpen question for the reviewer. Did the driver hold position inside the 50 m radius continuously for at least 180 seconds during 11:33:47 to 11:37:04? The rider's 37-second shortfall and the driver's 400-second run cannot both be right, and only a full-resolution GPS export (or the platform's own GPS_AUTO arrival and wait-timer records) can settle it. If the continuous dwell reached 180 seconds, the fee stands and POL-NS-07 fixes the driver's payout at 80 percent of SGD 4.50 = SGD 3.60. If it did not, POL-NS-06 refunds the SGD 4.50 in full with no compensation.\n\nNo referral is issued: no clause on these facts produces one."
