    "explanation": "Both of you filed on trip TRP-02756, and neither of you gets a money ruling today. The case goes to a human reviewer, and the $4.50 stays where it is - charged, not refunded, not released to the driver - until that reviewer decides. Here is why, and what each of you should know.\n\nWHAT IS SETTLED. The driver accepted at 11:28:17, pressed the arrival marker at 11:32:47, and cancelled at 11:39:28 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW (EV-TRIP-02756, weight 1.0). Nobody boarded. The chat log holds 0 messages and the trip carries no in-app calls (EV-CHAT-02756, weight 1.0). The fare ledger charges $4.50, which equals the cancellation fee in force for this trip (trip_record.platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd = $4.50), so there is no fare-integrity defect under POL-NS-08(d). There is no traffic advisory covering this pickup: EV-ADVIS-02756-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT.\n\nTHE QUESTION THAT DECIDES THE $4.50 is whether the driver held position inside the 50 m arrival radius for a continuous 180 seconds - the free waiting period in force, read from trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180 (POL-NS-01(c)). The 300 s figure in fee_schedule.minimum_dwell_sec applies only to records authored before policy version 2 and does not apply to this record, which carries its own platform_policy. On that question the record will not let me rule.\n\nTHE GAP, AND THE DRIVER'S CASE. EV-GPS-02756 has a 197-second sampling hole from 11:33:47 to 11:37:04, squarely inside the waiting window. That is longer than the 120-second threshold in POL-NS-08(b), so the trace is impaired at policy level, not merely flagged by the pre-pass: its weight is 0.39, from the issue codes GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW and LOW_COVERAGE (0.6 x 0.65). You are right, driver, that the trace shows 22 qualifying in-radius fixes, 203 seconds of observed in-radius time in two runs of 60 s and 143 s, and that no fix shows a departure - the straight-line displacement across the hole is 0.0 km and the maximum excursion is unmeasurable. But the same hole is the middle of your 400-second span from 11:32:47 to 11:39:27: the continuity of limb (c) cannot be read across it, so the 400 s run cannot be certified any more than the 143 s run can be certified as the whole dwell. Your claim that EV-TRIP-02756 is an independent second carrier fails the removal test: take the trace away and nothing in the trip record shows the driver inside the geofence - its wait timer runs from a BUTTON tap, and POL-NS-12 makes platform arrival and wait-timer events an independent carrier only for a GPS_AUTO arrival carrying those events in trip_record.events, which this record does not (events is null). POL-NS-01(c) deliberately measures the clock from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, not from the tap. Your statement that you waited the full time is noted but POL-NS-01(c) does not read a party statement. So the confidence cap is 0.39, not 1.0, and the $3.60 you claim under POL-NS-07 (0.8 x $4.50 = $3.60, arithmetic correct, anti-farming check not tripped: no_show_terminations_30d 0 against 85 completed trips in 30 days) is not paid on this ruling while chargeability itself is undecided. The alternative you offered - escalation on the 143 s reading - is the outcome, but for the reason below rather than the one you gave.\n\nTHE RIDER'S CASE. Your 143 seconds and your 37-second shortfall are a real reading of the same trace, and you are right that POL-NS-06(i) is unavailable: the advisory is MISSING and the derivation itself records advisory_missing and excursion_unmeasurable, so the two runs of 60 s and 143 s cannot be summed to 203 s and the 197 s hole cannot be scored as served waiting time. But this cuts both ways. The same trace cannot show that the driver left and re-entered either, so 143 s cannot be certified as the effective dwell any more than 400 s can. Limb (c) is undecided over the hole, not failed, and an undecided limb supports neither a charge that needs the clause to hold nor a refund that needs it to fail. Your full refund of $4.50 therefore cannot issue on this record, and neither can the charge be confirmed.\n\nWHAT YOUR OTHER CLAIMS SETTLED. POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider: limb (a) fails on an empty chat log, so the answered-message route is not reached (accepted, and it does not change the outcome). POL-NS-11: the absent rider track is neutral, it does not impair the driver's arrival and dwell evidence and it is not what sends this case to review (accepted). POL-NS-05 does not fire - the arrival marker coincides with the first qualifying in-radius fix at 11:32:47, offset 0.0 s, so there is no false-arrival finding and no POL-NS-05(ii) referral. No profile field drives this case: rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d are both 0, rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0, and driver_profile.prior_no_show_flags is a lifetime counter that POL-NS-09(d) does not read and that I have not used - it is context only under POL-GEN-01.\n\nWHY ESCALATE. Both sides' dwell claims rest on the same artifact, and that artifact is impaired under POL-NS-08(b). Under POL-GEN-02(2) confidence is capped by the weight of the artifact carrying the deciding fact - 0.39, with no independent second carrier - which is below the 0.70 floor, so the case escalates automatically under POL-NS-09(a); and independently, POL-NS-09(e) escalates because the sole evidence for the deciding fact is impaired. Escalation is terminal: no amount is refunded and none is released, and the execution threshold in POL-GEN-05 is not reached because no money moves on this ruling. No referral issues, because no clause produces one on these facts: POL-NS-05(ii) does not fire, and the POL-NS-07 instruction to direct a refund applies only where the anti-farming check trips, which it does not.\n\nWHAT THE REVIEWER MUST SETTLE. Whether the driver remained inside the 50 m arrival radius for the whole stretch 11:33:47 to 11:37:04. The natural record-type evidence is the platform's full-resolution GPS export for that interval. If the reviewer finds the driver held position, the $4.50 charge stands and the driver is paid $3.60; if the reviewer finds he did not, the $4.50 is refunded to the rider in full. Either party may ask for a human decision, and either may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
